From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: disable hw-rfkill polling on Radxa Orion O6/O6N

The RTL8852B WiFi chip on Radxa Orion O6 and O6N boards exhibits
spurious hw-rfkill state transitions during boot.  Polling rfkill
state on this chip on these specific boards is unreliable and adds
noise without any user-visible benefit.

Gate rtw89_chip_has_rfkill() to return false when the chip ID is
RTL8852B AND the DMI matches Radxa Orion O6 or Radxa Orion O6N.
Non-Orion systems, or Orion systems with a different WiFi chip, are
completely unaffected: both gates must be satisfied simultaneously.

Recommended for port by the Tier 3 examination -- small, in-tree,
narrowly scoped, with a precise DMI+chip-ID double gate.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  sys-kernel/cix-sources/files/80010-rtw89-disable-hw-rfkill-polling-on-orion-o6.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds;
 file context offset shifts due to our prior series expansion
 (7214 here vs 6427 in the upstream raw patch body)]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
index 68dad6090..88a5bf7b9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
@@ -7214,6 +7214,26 @@ static int rtw89_chip_board_info_setup(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
 
 static bool rtw89_chip_has_rfkill(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
 {
+	static const struct dmi_system_id no_hw_rfkill_dmi[] = {
+		{
+			.matches = {
+				DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Radxa Computer (Shenzhen) Co., Ltd."),
+				DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Radxa Orion O6"),
+			},
+		},
+		{
+			.matches = {
+				DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Radxa Computer (Shenzhen) Co., Ltd."),
+				DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Radxa Orion O6N"),
+			},
+		},
+		{ }
+	};
+
+	if (rtwdev->chip->chip_id == RTL8852B &&
+	    dmi_check_system(no_hw_rfkill_dmi))
+		return false;
+
 	return !!rtwdev->chip->rfkill_init;
 }
 
